<title>USA: CoCensys begins Phase II migraine trial.</title>
<headline>CoCensys begins Phase II migraine trial.</headline>
<dateline>IRVINE, Calif. 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>CoCensys Inc said it initiated a Phase II clinical trial of ganaxolone or CCD 1042, in patients who suffer from migraine headaches.</p>
<p>Unlike most other drugs for migraine which work to modulate the dilation in the blood vessels commonly believed to cause migraines, CoCensys' ganoxolone acts on the nerve endings attached to the blood vessels.  CoCensys said recent findings suggest the nerve endings release peptides that cause local inflammation and possibly are the source of the migraine pain.</p>
</text>
